\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The \texttt  {Evict} algorithm. Upon every data access operation, two buckets are chosen at every level of the tree for eviction during which one data block will be evicted to one of its children. To ensure security, a dummy eviction is performed for the child that does not receive a block; further, if the bucket chosen for eviction is empty, dummy evictions are performed on both child buckets. In this figure, \(R\) denotes a real eviction and \(D\) denotes a dummy eviction.}}{52}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
